<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore mulls new soft commodities regulations.</title>
<headline>Singapore mulls new soft commodities regulations.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's finance minister Richard Hu said on Tuesday the city-state would consider drafting laws to regulate soft commodities trading, state television reported.</p>
<p>Hu said in response to a question in Parliament that the government is thinking of such laws to stop firms who trick Singaporeans by promising them very high returns, television said.</p>
<p>Legislation would be used to &quot;regulate the activities&quot; of these companies, the report said. No further details were immediately available.</p>
